**Theorem 11.1 (exact finite boundary).** Fix $P$ and $N\ge1$.
There is an exact deterministic realization on all edges
$\mathcal C^-_{P,N}\to\mathcal C_{P,N}$ with exactly $N$
supplemental values. Thus the least supplemental alphabet for this
chart is $N$ for both exact contracts of Definition 10.1. Its
fixed-width binary encoding requires and attains
$\lceil\log_2N\rceil$ logical bits, in addition to $O^+$ and the fixed
mathematical parameters $P,N$.

Proof. Use $Z_N=\{0,\ldots,N-1\}$ and set
$z(s_{N,m,k})=m$ throughout that branch. This assignment is well-defined:
the histories on different branches contain different supplied payloads,
and different cut indices have different receipt tallies. More strongly,

$$
\eta_N(s_{N,m,k})=\bigl(O^+(s_{N,m,k}),m\bigr)
$$

is injective on the entire chart. Equality of its second coordinates
gives the same $m$. Equality of its full meters then gives
$n_{P,N}+k=n_{P,N}+k'$, hence $k=k'$. With $P,N,m$ fixed, actual
deterministic execution after the specified finite input has exactly
one such cut. This deals with later-cut collisions; initial-fibre
injectivity alone would not suffice.

Let $A_N=\eta_N(\mathcal C_{P,N})$ and
$A^-_N=\eta_N(\mathcal C^-_{P,N})$. Injectivity makes the following
actual descended update a function:

$$
T_N\bigl(\eta_N(s_{N,m,k})\bigr)
   =\eta_N(s_{N,m,k+1}),\qquad k<D_{P,N}.
$$

Equivalently, on this realized domain $m$ selects the branch. Writing
$\operatorname{receipts}(o)$ for the meter's receipt count already
present in $o=O^+(s)$ identifies
$k=\operatorname{receipts}(o)-n_{P,N}$. The equation supplies one and only one
successor there, preserving its complete projected native record.
Induction gives exactly the required singleton response set at every
permitted horizon. Treating this graph as a nondeterministic graph
therefore also attains its exact contract. Theorem 10.2's fixed-$N$
lower bound proves sharpness; counting binary words gives the stated
width, including width zero for $N=1$.

The domain of $T_N$ is $A^-_N$, not all pairs $(o,m)$. In particular,
no update or original `none` is assigned at a last chart cut: its
actual next edge belongs to the forward import outside the selected
chart. No extension to that import, parsing, binding, another request,
or all $N$ follows from this construction. The mathematical function
uses actual finite histories to define its graph; it installs no table,
advice, extractor, runtime history access or new row engine. ∎

